// DAZ Studio filetype DAZ Script
/*
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.44 - UI read-scope reuse for inventory and materials
 * PERF: one synchronous read scope now covers readOutfitSummary + card
 * diagnostics. Inventory maps and material snapshots are reused inside that
 * scope only (still discarded on Scene.update / metadata writes / scope end).
 * Overlapping Worn sets no longer re-walk the same garment materials N times
 * during dialog open/refresh. Scene semantics and verification are unchanged.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.43 - compact Settings, Debug Mode and editor footer spacing
 * Based on the user-edited v0.9.10.42(1); wardrobe and material transactions preserved.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.42 - New/Edit Outfit and Manage Groups UI polish
 * Set Editor: screen-work-area aware height/position; green/gray scope buttons;
 * wrapped icon caption; Georgia property controls, compact item bulk buttons;
 * gold item labels and fixed green/red action footer.
 * Manage Groups: collapsed-by-default expandable members; colored actions.
 * User-edited v0.9.10.41(1) interface is the base; scene operations unchanged.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.41 - Wardrobe polish and multi-Replacement editor
 * UI: gold item labels, 120px Move Selected icon/text button, compact Replace
 * dialog with true multi-select and preserved reciprocal policy support.
 * PERF: catalog-only transition changes skip unrelated scene undo/selection
 * snapshots, and update only in-memory button state without re-inventory.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.40 - Wardrobe Transition inline selector and Replace picker
 * UI: per-item Remove / Keep / Replace are mutually exclusive green/gray
 * button-style radio choices. Replace enables a separate "..." picker with
 * same-figure-type registered item choices, Save Policy / Cancel actions.
 * Catalog edits retain existing transaction/commit/stale checks. Ordinary
 * store/restore arrows and Move Selected are unchanged.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.39 - 32x32 Restore Materials / Restore Properties icon buttons
 * UI: replace main Set-card text restoration buttons with icon-only controls
 *     from Resources. Keep the existing click handlers, guards, and tooltips.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.38 - Georgia text, compact cards and clear material restore
 * UI: all Wardrobe Sets windows use Georgia for labels, inputs and buttons.
 * UI: top-aligned Georgia titles, italic figure/Label scope and tight 5px-ish
 *     icon gutters on main outfit cards (extra height only for status).
 * UI: remove diagnostic-only Details button. Keep the actionable manual
 *     native material restore as clearly labelled Restore Materials...
 * UI: concise Create Variant prompt without any copy-of-scene wording.
 * UI: single toolbar Edit / Duplicate / Partial Set / Take Off Set / | / Delete.
 * Keep previous user icon styling and DAZ4/DAZ6 transaction safeguards.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.36 - DAZ4 composite Saved Set proof, single partial status
 * Per-Set visibility for registered parts; PartID-scoped numeric/Boolean
 * properties; Partial Apply, Worn/Modified status and verified rollback.
 * Original registered Items and their DUF presets remain immutable.
 * FIX: a Set material preset on a registered GeoShell can expose both a
 * zero/unmapped DrawStyleOverride and a zero/unmapped Displacement Adaptive
 * Quality. Independently prove each complete native value/map pair; require
 * Iray Uber and unchanged displacement strength/map for Adaptive Quality.
 * All other material differences and native rollback remain fully strict.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.31 - DAZ6 Saved Set native GeoShell neutral-property proof (2026-10-11)
 * FIX: allow DAZ6.25's newly exposed zero/unmapped Iray fields only on an
 * natively attached GeoGraft and its registered children, after an explicit
 * native Set material restore. Verify each native field and all remaining
 * material values; preserve strict rollback and other wearable comparisons.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.29 - Source Picker & Native Shell Import (2026-10-11)
 * UI: restore action icons INSIDE buttons using sizedFromIcon=true; add 10px
 * footer separation. Skip source picker if no transferable source survived
 * strict discovery, even if scene contains registered but blocked candidates.
 * FIX: on DAZ 6.25, import-only GeoShell UV ordinal differences plus absent
 * complete donor GeoGraft surface groups may be proved from a fresh native
 * material/UV observation. No setter and no relaxation of ordinary materials,
 * unrelated shader values, actual pose snapshots or rollback comparisons.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.28 - Composite Replacement & Source Picker Layout (2026-10-11)
 * FIX: Composite variant creation now recognizes both replacement and removal
 * of previously registered children. Old definitions and Sets remain immutable;
 * detached, still-tagged old children and changed surviving native references
 * still fail closed. Pre-editor hierarchy problems receive concise messages,
 * full details are printed to DAZ Log.
 * UI: Choose Sources uses real 38px icon-only buttons next to clickable text
 * buttons, avoiding native scaled-down icons inside text buttons. Footer is
 * 10px vertically padded, anchored tightly to the content, with no blank
 * area below Cancel/Continue.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.27 - Source Picker & Composite Variants (2026-10-11)
 * UI: Choose Sources has green/gray mutually exclusive choice buttons,
 * larger explicit action icons, and green Continue/red Cancel, matching
 * the Partial Sets footer. No transfer decision is made until Continue.
 * NEW: Registered active item with newly parented, untagged descendants
 * offers an EXPLICIT fork into a new, immutable composite item definition
 * before opening Set Editor. The original catalog item and all Sets are
 * left unchanged; the new variant receives its own Item/Variant/Part IDs,
 * portable references and native wearable preset. Foreign tagged nodes,
 * split/foreign parts, outstanding material snapshots and active item overrides
 * remain blocked; genuine removed/replaced parts can form NEW variants. Preset/export failures retain metadata for rollback.
 * matew Wardrobe Sets v0.9.10.26 - Verification Setting Consistency (2026-10-11)
 * PERF FIX v0.9.10.26: Partial Set Apply now honors the explicitly
 * selected Operational profile, just like ordinary Apply, Undress All,
 * bulk/individual Wardrobe moves and Take Off Set. This reduces ordinary
 * pre/post observation windows and skips whole-human pose snapshots, but
 * keeps full item/material/link checks, and independently conservative
 * material-recheck/rollback observation. Save/Edit/unregister and explicit
 * diagnostic actions intentionally remain conservative maintenance.
 * PERF FIX v0.9.10.26: When Optimized reads is enabled AND Full is
 * selected (or an action is maintenance), pose snapshots now use the
 * existing figure-own-bones-only linear traversal. It has the same node
 * ownership and output fields as the legacy full descendant traversal;
 * with Optimized reads unchecked the legacy reader remains intact.
 * Profile/policy source and actual pose walker are explicitly diagnosed.
 * UI FIX v0.9.10.25: Wardrobe item labels receive an explicit content
 * width rather than a size-hint-limited QLabel: long registered names
 * can use the actual available horizontal space and wrap onto two rows.
 * Per-card Take Off Set no longer opens a redundant confirmation: it still
 * runs the same safe single transaction, preflight, and rollback checks.
 * Only these two presentation/interaction details changed in this version.
 * NEW v0.9.10.24: The Wardrobe window is wider for complete item names;
 * existing single-arrow controls are unchanged, and each active/stored
 * item now has an initially-clear checkbox. Move Selected validates all
 * chosen directions/instance IDs before a SINGLE transient Apply plan and
 * verifies every original item/location afterward. Its durable rollback,
 * GeoGraft material snapshots and native link safety remain mandatory.
 * NEW v0.9.10.24: Per-card Take Off Set stores only worn members of that
 * particular saved Set, regardless of their Keep/Replace transition rules.
 * Applied figure PropertyState is Reset and cleared within the same pending
 * transaction. Unrelated registered clothes and unregistered nodes are kept.
 * OPERATIONAL Wardrobe single/batch movement uses the same short ordinary
 * observation windows as Apply (Full still performs full diagnostics). Bulk
 * movement avoids repeated separate preflight/report/rollback transactions.
 * GeoGraft and material verification remains unchanged. New per-operation
 * verification profile and timing are recorded in Last Report.
 * FIX v0.9.10.23: DAZ4 4.24 native import of a registered GeoShell
 * can combine three separate proven differences in ONE item: a locally
 * renumbered but identically named UV Set (Base Female 7 -> 6), absent
 * zero/unmapped viewport DrawStyleOverride controls on non-Iray shell
 * surfaces, and whole donor-only Nipples surface groups missing because
 * the recipient does not wear that graft. A legacy importer classifier
 * alone cannot establish the combination. Only in the native imported
 * shell material check, require the live shell to target the selected
 * figure, a fresh second snapshot identical to the observed snapshot,
 * a fresh unique native material/property list, named-UV native values,
 * and the existing guarded missing-donor topology proof; then reuse the
 * same full remaining-field comparison as Set material restoration.
 * Never change native material values, the catalog, presets, transfer
 * logic, ordinary wearable compatibility or strict scene/rollback checks.
 * Log each proven accepted difference and reject incomplete evidence.
 * FIX v0.9.10.23: Saved Set material verification after a native
 * GeoShell preset load has a separate path from initial native import.
 * When its original strict/native-import classifier fails on DAZ4 4.24,
 * perform an independent, read-only proof for missing zero/unmapped
 * DrawStyleOverride (a viewport control) on live native Geometry Shell
 * surfaces. Require unique live material/property names, native absence,
 * exact neutral saved values and fully matching remaining shader fields.
 * Displacement Adaptive Quality retains the stronger Iray shader and
 * unchanged-displacement checks. Absent donor-graft surface groups require
 * their existing topology proof; UV enum ordinal projection requires its
 * existing independent name/control check. This bounded fallback applies
 * ONLY to restoring a Saved Set, never to ordinary wearables, other DAZ
 * runtimes, source catalog, live scene snapshots or transaction rollback.
 * Report acceptance and concrete rejected proof details separately.
 * FIX v0.9.10.21: DAZ 4.24 may enumerate the very same named UV set
 * with a different numeric index than the saved DAZ 6.25 JSON baseline
 * (observed: Base Female = 7 in snapshot, 6 in DAZ4). Never try to
 * force the saved ordinal into a different runtime's DzEnumProperty.
 * For Set material comparison/restore ONLY, treat a cross-runtime
 * numeric UV ordinal as compatible after independently confirming the
 * matching nonempty UV name, fresh native UV control and native/current
 * numeric value on the selected figure's registered GeoShell. Project
 * only that ordinal in a disposable comparison snapshot; all other
 * properties, maps, UV names, donor topology and shaders are strictly
 * verified. No edits to the saved catalog or measured rollback state.
 * The existing DAZ4 missing-neutral-field rule keeps its own fresh
 * native proof, even if unrelated shader controls were unreadable.
 * FIX v0.9.10.20: WM2 icon rendering no longer depends on a successful
 * WM2Support include(). Use the already-validated WM2 Settings icon rules,
 * legacy Wearable Manager.json name/class maps, and WM2-compatible builtin
 * classifications when runtime resolver is unavailable. Native nodes remain
 * read-only; catalog-only items cannot invent missing Asset IDs.
 * FIX v0.9.10.20: Set Editor content lives in an outer scroll area and
 * dialog height is capped for DAZ 4/6 rather than expanding beyond the screen.
 * FIX v0.9.10.19: Set Editor resolves icon sources for saved item IDs
 * that are not on the selected figure (e.g. already transferred to another
 * figure) through a read-only scene-wide ItemRoot lookup. Only a separate
 * iconNodeKey is populated; the editor's action/material nodeKey remains
 * local to the selected figure. When no instance exists anywhere, use a
 * transient WM2-compatible catalog icon proxy (saved item name and root
 * node class), never creating scene nodes or changing catalog metadata.
 * Choose Sources and Registered Items use the same resolution path.
 * FIX v0.9.10.18: protect the DAZ 4.24 native import of registered
 * GeoShells whose snapshots include unreadable shader fields. For a
 * Geometry Shell natively targeting the selected figure ONLY, permit the
 * existing two named DAZ4 absent-zero/unmapped Iray controls to be judged
 * independently even if the snapshot's unrelated fields were skipped.
 * Require a fresh native material class/shader and property-list proof on
 * EVERY affected surviving surface; all comparable other fields, maps and
 * UV values must still match. Only the existing guarded donor GeoGraft
 * group classifier can account for fully absent additional shell surfaces.
 * This is import-only compatibility, NOT a change to measured scene state,
 * stored records, native presets, rollback, or a claim to verify skipped
 * fields. Unknown, incomplete native proofs and partial donor groups FAIL.
 * FIX v0.9.10.17: Choose Sources icon rows now pass the live source
 * root node to the shared WM2 icon resolver. WM2 Menu applies icon rules
 * to an actual DzNode; passing only a catalogue name and empty nodeKey
 * skipped all configured name/label/asset-ID rules. Source lookup is
 * read-only and icon references are UI-only (not transfer decisions).
 * FIX v0.9.10.16: permit one already-worn, natively attached recipient
 * GeoGraft to be moved into its own Wardrobe as part of an otherwise valid
 * same-type incoming single-GeoGraft transfer. This is the existing protected
 * Store -> Transfer transaction, not a new unbacked path. Refuse recipient
 * graft Restore/Load or multiple simultaneously stored grafts in this mode.
 * Before mutation, all source and target GeoShell native/property backups
 * and target graft-specific Wardrobe material snapshots must be prepared.
 * Check after transfer that the recipient's outgoing GeoGraft is detached,
 * stored and retains its exact immutable material-snapshot pointer.
 * No relaxation of source attachment, material coverage or verified rollback.
 * FIX: update displayed VERSION constant (v0.9.10.15 still displayed .14).
 * FIX: recapture live GeoShell JSON/native presets when an existing Set is
 * edited with its donor GeoGraft attached. Preserve old baselines for stored
 * donors and missing shells, rather than overwriting them with incomplete
 * topology. Enforce same live topology for any registered_full references.
 * FIX: correct DAZ native UV Set enum re-binding on registered GeoShells
 * after applying Set or temporary rollback presets; reverify every exposed
 * material field and retain strict pre-existing diff/rollback checks.
 * FIX: reject single-node registered GeoShell native presets whose material
 * surface list cannot cover their JSON snapshots. No silent omissions.
 * FIX v0.9.10.14: a valid material of an existing destination GeoShell
 * may be returned by getAllMaterials() but silently omitted from native
 * DzMaterialAssetFilter output (confirmed: Breast Utilities 2 Shell (2),
 * Body). Separate native export also omits the material entirely. For
 * TEMPORARY transaction rollback ONLY, capture the missing surface using
 * DAZ's own DzProperty.addValueToSettings (incl. default/current values and
 * texture images), store its original UV and unique shader-property names,
 * and restore via DzProperty.setValueFromSettings ONLY if rollback needs it.
 * Verify original available material state after native segment imports and
 * before commit. If DAZ does not expose complete property settings, abort
 * before any figure transfer. No manual shader-value reconstruction or
 * omissions treated as native backup success. This path is experimental and
 * must be validated in actual DAZ Studio on a saved scene COPY.
 * FIX: Choose Sources already offers live registered items kept in Wardrobe,
 * but GeoGraft transfer preflight rejected a valid stored GeoGraft even when
 * Recovery proved it belonged to the source figure. Support one stored,
 * natively DETACHED GeoGraft with optional registered active/stored GeoShells
 * using the same dual-owner material backups and rollback transaction. A
 * stored graft must not be reattached to the source as a hidden side effect.
 * Its source GeoShells have no disappearing graft surfaces, so require exact
 * unchanged source materials rather than using worn-graft allowances.
 * Worn GeoGrafts still MUST be truly native-attached at preflight. Inconsistent
 * stored/attached or worn/detached states fail before any scene mutation.
 * FIX: DAZ native material export may omit one selected GeoShell surface
 * (observed: Body) from an otherwise valid full rollback preset. For temporary
 * transaction backups only, capture the missing surfaces in separate strictly
 * verified native material presets, and restore all segments before comparing
 * the whole original material snapshot. Never waive surface coverage or
 * treat a failed native split export as a successful backup. No scene mutation
 * is performed until all affected source/target shell backups are complete.
 * NEW: before any GeoGraft is detached into Wardrobe, capture the named,
 * graft-owned GeoShell surfaces as independently verified native selective
 * material DUFs and a durable immutable manifest in Materials/. A pointer and
 * per-shell pending list travel with the stored scene instance (own metadata).
 * Return Registered Item, full and partial Apply consume that pointer after
 * restoring topology; native material readback checks selected + unrelated
 * surfaces, UVs and available values. Saved Sets retain style precedence.
 * Changing local graft topology during an ordinary-clothing multi-owner
 * transfer now uses the same target shell rollback backups and capture path.
 * Existing stored grafts without a pre-store manifest cannot be reconstructed
 * from material data already lost. Recreate these tests from a saved source scene.
 * DAZ 4.24 / 6.25 native on-scene tests remain REQUIRED; do not overwrite source scenes.
 *
 * FIX: during GeoGraft transfer, locally stored destination GeoShells are
 * valid members queued for Wardrobe Restore before the incoming GeoGraft.
 * Their native target is verified; stored shells on either figure receive
 * topology-safe backup/recovery, not just currently worn shells.
 * PREVIOUS FIX: registered GeoShell imports and saved Set styles can have donor-only
 * graft surface groups absent from the target figure. Detect those groups
 * by native shell topology + consistent graft surface prefixes, retaining
 * strict checks of all present material values and unrelated diffs.
 * The immutable catalog and native material presets are NEVER rewritten;
 * skipped donor-only surfaces are reported as NOT exactly verified.
 * NEW: opt-in one-GeoGraft + registered GeoShell transfer from the same owner,
 * with native Shell Node retarget and guarded reverse retarget on rollback.
 * NEW: Partial Sets carry snapshots of selected GeoGrafts only; missing
 * target GeoShells are skipped, while existing compatible ones are restored.
 * Partial Sets do not offer cross-figure Source Picker in this version.
 * PREVIOUS: opt-in one-active-GeoGraft transfer between two figures with existing
 * GeoShells; preflight on both figures, dual-owner material backups, source
 * unaffected-surface verification and restore on destination. No GeoShell
 * transfers in the same action. DAZ scene-copy validation is REQUIRED.
 * FIX: GeoShell safety opt-out is an expected non-error block; users may
 * open Settings from its informational dialog, without FAIL/Stopped reporting.
 * NEW: strictly opt-in experimental GeoShell material restore on normal Apply,
 * backed up before topology changes, restoring stored Set baselines after
 * the GeoGraft returns. Registered GeoShells reuse their full native DUF.
 * Target-local simultaneous graft changes and partial cross-figure source
 * selection remain excluded until separately validated.
 * Warning: this is NOT a complete scene/Undo guarantee; use ONLY a saved COPY.
 * Native DAZ Save/Import probes remain available in Settings for diagnostics.
 * Independent namespace and storage; own logical IDs, durable NodeID references.
 * Based on the supplied Wearables Manager reference and tested Switch Probe v0.2.
 * Save-filter pattern: Daz 3D "Save a Wearable(s) Preset"
 * https://docs.daz3d.com/public/software/dazstudio/4/referenceguide/scripting/api_reference/samples/file_io/save_duf_wearables/start
 * Sample attribution/license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
 *
 * v0.9.6: persistent per-item Remove/Keep/Replace policies; optional,
 * explicitly confirmed reverse replacements; independently matched co-worn
 * sets; partial Keep All/Follow Rules/Take Off All; Take Off All confirmation.
 * Every plan still uses native item IDs, Recovery, validation and rollback.
 * No simulation presence detection or cache-specific behavior. No transform,
 * smoothing, pose or simulation-property writes during wardrobe switching.
 * v0.9.4.1: Set cards evaluate live material snapshots independently of the last
 * applied Set, without changing what counts as wearing its registered clothes.
 * First-time Save Materials may capture the stored registered scene instance.
 * v0.9.4: A full Apply may restore a set-specific native Material Preset when
 * saved materials differ; JSON-only presets warn and remain untouched. This is
 * transactional batch restoration, not guaranteed native DAZ Undo. Partial
 * Sets deliberately never auto-restore materials.
 * Uses native parenting, Fit To, collision links and observational settling.
 * v0.3.2: named/typed material diffs persisted before rollback; one bounded
 * read-only material recheck on mismatch, with the unchanged catalog baseline.
 * v0.3.3: limited DAZ 4.24 Iray import compatibility for two absent zero-valued
 * properties with empty maps. Displacement exception additionally requires
 * disabled, unmapped displacement. Every omission is retained and warned about;
 * compatibility is NOT exact equality or a claim of identical rendering.
 * Current-scene before/after comparisons stay strict. No value coercion or
 * tolerance relaxation. Existing catalog snapshots are never edited by this rule.
 * v0.3.4: reuse the stateless native property helper; short-lived read indexes
 * are discarded between phases and invalidated on own metadata writes.
 * No node/property/value cache spans Scene.update(), sleep(), or processEvents().
 * Single-pass snapshot differences keep the existing numeric tolerance.
 * Both optimized and reference engines retain every original validation stage.
 * Performance summaries measure native runs; no DAZ speedup claimed beforehand.
 * v0.3.5: standard transform control accessors resolved once per snapshot,
 * with direct optional-property reads and bounded sampled stage profiling.
 * No observation policy, material import compatibility, rollback or scope change.
 * v0.3.6: per-node native-accessor certification, then a fresh property list
 * per snapshot; signal-invalidated binding descriptors contain no values or
 * DzProperty wrappers. Native-accessor audits after quiet windows. Unknown
 * node/property types use the unchanged v0.3.5 reader; no guessed zeroes.
 * v0.3.7: replace JS property-wrapper equality with the documented owner/name
 * uniqueness contract. Check both wrappers' native class/owner/flags, exclude
 * private-name collisions, and cross-check fresh channel state at certification
 * and every post-observation audit. Actual bulk usage and failure details logged.
 * v0.3.8: explicit, opt-in OPERATIONAL verification profile for Apply actions.
 * It retains item snapshots, material comparisons, identities/recovery, pose
 * boundary comparisons, observation tolerances and rollback. It polls the figure
 * root and every registered non-bone part, NOT every human bone on each sample;
 * repeated dual-reader self-audits are omitted in ordinary Apply windows only.
 * This is an explicit COVERAGE change, not a claim of identical diagnostics.
 * FULL (default) keeps v0.3.7 polling/audits. No cache of property values is added.
 * v0.3.9: Operational-only linear own-bone traversal, same pose snapshot fields.
 * Optional script-lifetime reuse of previously certified plain channel bindings
 * for consecutive Apply actions on the same figure/catalog. Fresh lists, owners,
 * classes, values and native field reads on every snapshot; never cache values.
 * Scene-list/clear and node property-layout signals invalidate retained bindings.
 * Full/reference paths keep per-action certification. First run remains cold.
 * v0.3.10: separate named observation policies. Ordinary Operational Apply
 * uses 8ms polling / 80ms quiet window / one required matching sample.
 * Full, material rechecks, rollback and maintenance use independent conservative
 * policy objects (80 / 800 / 5). Actual per-window thresholds are logged.
 * Operational no-op uses fresh structural preflight and desired-state validation
 * BEFORE any settling, measurement, pose snapshot, or wardrobe write. It does
 * NOT claim geometry/material/pose stability; Full retains diagnostic no-op.
 * No library/schema migration.
 * v0.3.11: no whole-human-figure pose snapshots/comparisons in Operational
 * Apply, including native import, material-recheck follow-up and rollback.
 * Full and maintenance retain pose diagnostics. Figure-root/item observation,
 * identity/owner/native links, material comparisons, frame guard and recovery
 * remain; no false TARGET_POSE pass is emitted. No viewport suppression,
 * metadata-index optimization, observation threshold or wardrobe schema change.
 * v0.4.0: persistent local UI settings, in-dialog Apply/status/filter/cards;
 * optional OFF-by-default native global viewport redraw lock around the
 * store/restore batch only. Released in finally BEFORE post-observation.
 * Short paired reference-lookup scopes end before EVERY native setter.
 * No catalog/scene schema migration or broader cache lifetime. v0.3.11 baseline
 * retained separately. Native v0.4.0 execution/layout/speedup not yet tested.
 * v0.4.1: batch adjacent synchronous metadata reads; build all three identity
 * indexes in one full-scene pass per read scope. Group creation, setters, native
 * import and event processing stay OUTSIDE these scopes. Metadata writes still
 * discard every scope index, including failed writes; no action/session cache.
 * Duplicate matches, native metadata schema validation, observation policies,
 * viewport lock lifecycle, figure-pose policy and wardrobe formats are unchanged.
 * v0.4.2: self-contained standard icon gallery and two-list membership editor.
 * Built-in art is materialized only in a local preview cache, then saved as a
 * normal relative PNG library asset on Save. No catalog schema migration.
 * Search/bulk-selection is editor-local; hidden selections are preserved.
 * Switching, recovery, observation, metadata engines and viewport lock unchanged.
 * v0.4.3: retain the existing DAZ 4.24 missing-property import rule and add
 * a separate DAZ 6.25 rule for ONLY two extra zero/unmapped Iray controls.
 * Extra adaptive quality requires disabled/unmapped displacement on both sides.
 * Exact snapshots/catalog/materials stay unchanged; additions and omissions are
 * reported separately. No new property-default, rendering or ownership claim.
 * Read-only candidate coverage is logged before planned imports and on Inspect.
 * Unmanaged clothes are NOT adopted, retagged, removed or matched by label.
 * v0.4.4: Take Off All Registered Items uses a transient empty target and the
 * existing Apply preflight/store/Recovery/observation/rollback path. The target
 * is never saved as a set. Current figure/current library only; unmanaged roots
 * and other owners are not adopted or detached. Already stored items remain.
 * Operational remains pose-free and keeps structural no-op; Full retains its
 * diagnostic profile. Added final checks preserve every original item identity.
 * v0.5.0: explicit per-outfit sources; separate copies default, same-instance
 * transfer between compatible owners is opt-in. Multi-owner pending/rollback.
 * External Shell/Rigid retargets excluded; internal dependencies preserved.
 * v0.5.1: source UI distinguishes items worn by a donor from items stored
 * in that donor's Wardrobe Sets storage; transfer engine semantics unchanged.
 * v0.5.2 FINAL TEST CANDIDATE: advisory numbered-label collision warning before
 * activating a registered item. Labels remain display-only and never establish
 * identity, reuse, removal, adoption, or skip decisions. Core engine unchanged.
 * v0.5.3 FINAL TEST PATCH: DAZ 4 parser-safe access to DzPushButton.default.
 * DAZ 6.25 import compatibility accepts only an EXTRA, fresh-API-confirmed
 * Displacement Adaptive Quality = 0 with no map; 0 requests no additional adaptive
 * subdivision. Existing catalog/runtime properties and all other material diffs stay strict.
 * v0.5.4 FINAL TEST PATCH: Registered Items maintenance can return stored items and
 * explicitly unregister only scene instances referenced by zero saved sets. Unregister
 * deletes this manager's scene metadata after restoring the item to the figure; historical
 * item/preset files are retained. Editor entry refreshes the catalog so a second DAZ
 * session cannot make the main-window snapshot silently stale; the in-editor stale guard remains.
 * A finite quiet window is not a native all-jobs-complete guarantee.
 * Immutable catalog revisions do not promise fsync/crash-atomic scene+disk transactions.
 * v0.6.0: production UI pass on the user-validated v0.5.4 core (20/20 final
 * test checklist passed in native DAZ testing). Main workflow is figure + outfit
 * cards; diagnostic controls move to Settings; editor, source chooser and registered
 * item maintenance are reorganized. Wardrobe engine/schema are intentionally frozen.
 * v0.7.0: set-level property overrides for figure controls and logical item-root
 * controls. Each override stores explicit Apply and Reset values. A direct Set A ->
 * Set B transition does not Reset properties managed by both sets; B is applied
 * directly. Properties no longer managed by the new set use A's stored Reset value.
 * Native UI layout of v0.6.0 passed DAZ 4/6 smoke testing.
 * v0.6.1: horizontal scene-figure strip with editable supported-figure profiles,
 * per-scene-figure custom icons (file or two-step Iray camera render), scope-priority
 * set ordering/borders, icon-first set cards, and maintenance/report actions moved
 * into Settings. Compatible-only display is now unconditional. Core wardrobe,
 * transfer, material, rollback and registration engines remain unchanged.
 * v0.8.0: outfit-worn is determined by the complete active registered-item
 * membership, independently of edited, missing, or unapplied native property
 * overrides. Read-only live property checks identify Modified/Missing values.
 * Restore Properties is a guarded, Apply-values-only action with preflight,
 * readback verification, carried-forward property bookkeeping and rollback.
 * No unrelated Reset values or registered garments are written. New override
 * Apply defaults to the live value if non-default, else native maximum.
 * Saved catalogs, PropertyState format and wearables ownership are unchanged.
 * v0.8.0.1: Edit Set shows 24x24 Edit badges for items with property overrides;
 * badges update when the Properties editor returns. DAZ 4: figure-selection
 * arrow is encoded as an ASCII source escape, not a literal UTF-8 glyph.
 * Custom figure icon bindings synchronize through an append-only, library-
 * local event journal so separate DAZ 4/6 preference directories can share
 * explicit Label/Specific icon assignments. No catalog/scene schema change.
 * v0.8.0.2: Missing/unresolvable native property overrides are advisory
 * during Apply/Take Off All, never a cause to abort otherwise valid outfit
 * changes. Warn after successful Apply; keep records for later repair.
 * Set Properties highlights unresolved loaded controls red and asks whether
 * to delete them on close. Edit Set shows 24px Missing Property artwork.
 * v0.9.0.5: place Take Off Current Outfit INSIDE Currently Worn scroll content,
 * immediately after the current registered wardrobe rows. No behavior change.
 * v0.9.1.3: DAZ 4 storage-ID collision remediation, explicit opt-in before
 * outfit transitions. Retires only rigorously validated EMPTY duplicate
 * storage groups by changing their own Role, and changes their NodeID only
 * if duplicated. The one populated storage, clothes and figure stay untouched.
 * Changes participate in current-action metadata rollback; never silently
 * merge/delete storage or bypass strict durable Recovery node lookup.
 * v0.9.1.2: DAZ 4 duplicate storage ID exception ONLY for one populated
 * group plus verified empty groups of the same figure/library. Never retag,
 * delete, or merge, and do not relax global node/figure/item ID safety.
 * v0.9.1.1: diagnose duplicated per-figure storage groups; only when
 * exactly one group contains children and the others are genuinely empty,
 * use the populated group without deleting or retagging anything.
 * Otherwise preserve the hard safety guard with group details.
 * v0.9.1: per-set, per-item optional read-only material snapshots saved in
 * immutable JSON catalog revisions. Native material comparison diagnostics only;
 * no automatic material application or shader writes during full/partial Apply.
 * v0.9.0.4: unified custom footer controls, Currently Worn removal checkbox,
 * compact content-driven Partial Sets dialog height.
 * v0.9.0.3: compact three-column Partial Sets UI, centered color-coded
 * headings and 120x32 selection buttons using transparent PNG backgrounds.
 * Currently Worn is a read-only active registered-item snapshot.
 * v0.9.0.2: read and validate the shared Wearable Manager Settings.json directly,
 * without relying on DAZ include() or a possibly stale WM2Support global.
 * Preserve WM2 defaults for a missing config, fail closed on invalid files.
 * v0.9.0.1: repair WM2 supported-figure lookup for a named Genesis figure:
 * use its configured canonical DzFigure objectName when present, otherwise
 * the explicit WM2 internal name; keep both managers' item data independent.
 * Display the WM2 load failure reason instead of a silent empty figure list.
 * v0.9.0: Partial Sets dialog for per-item and per-property selection.
 * Reuses the native set planner with a transient target; separate, merged
 * PropertyState (no false full-set bookkeeping), optional Take Off Current.
 * v0.8.1.1: fail closed on corrupt WM2 settings, cached figure-type checks,
 * and WM2 protected-children exclusions in the wardrobe candidates list.
 * v0.9.3.7: checkbox multi-selection for native material restore; preflight
 * and temporary native backups for ALL selected items precede all loads.
 * Batch restores all attempted items on error, leaving failed backups on disk.
 * Native Undo participation remains unverified; no undo guarantee.
 * v0.9.5: Settings > Copy Library creates a verified, byte-for-byte
 * backup of the entire active library in an existing empty folder.
 * The write lock prevents normal concurrent Wardrobe Sets commits; its
 * transient .matew-write-lock directory is excluded from the backup.
 * Source/path/catalog IDs and active Settings are never switched or edited.
 * Read-only scan rejects symlinks and paths outside the library root.
 * Missing files or verification failure leave a flagged incomplete copy,
 * never delete or overwrite existing user files.
 * v0.9.3.8: DAZ 4.24 Iray material import compatibility now permits a missing
 * zero/unmapped Displacement Adaptive Quality even where the surface has no
 * Displacement Strength channel (e.g. imported hair ties). Any existing
 * displacement inputs must still match the saved snapshot; every other
 * property/map difference remains blocking. No catalog or scene data rewritten.
 * v0.9.8: Copy Library prechecks an empty destination before confirmation,
 * shows a cancellable native progress dialog for copy/verification, and uses
 * C++ ByteArray hex block comparisons instead of per-byte JavaScript loops.
 * Progress and the owned library lock are closed in finally on normal failure
 * or cancellation. A process kill can still leave the on-disk lock behind;
 * stale lock cleanup is never automatic.
 * v0.9.8: optional group-scoped outfit switching plus compact New Group and
 * safe Save Set Before Camera. Older sets retain whole-wardrobe transitions.
 * v0.9.10.5: experimental opt-in native material recovery during full Apply,
 * with per-operation full shell backups, conservative matching by name/asset
 * ID and native UV correction. No automatic graft transfer between figures
 * with GeoShells yet. Live DAZ topology and rollback tests are REQUIRED.
 * v0.9.10.4: immutable GeoGraft/GeoShell surface material references captured
 * into Set. GeoShells saved as full members reuse the same native preset.
 * v0.9.9.2: New/Rename Group prompt uses symmetric horizontal spacing and
 * the matching custom green/red Partial Sets action button styling.
 * v0.9.9: Group Manager (create/rename/delete; moved to Set Editor in 0.9.9.1).
 * v0.9.7: cosmetic outfit groups. An optional groupID on Set records and
 * a catalog-local groups collection, with old sets treated as Default.
 * Filtering is UI-only; groups never affect Apply, transitions, material
 * restore, Worn status, registration, or figure ownership.
 * v0.8.1: catalog-only Duplicate Set (fresh ID, shared registered items,
 * copied scope/properties/icon) and shared WM2 figure-type configuration.
 * Older figure types remain valid for catalog reading. The legacy type list
 * is a fallback only when Wearable Manager Support.dsa is unavailable.
 */
